      "card_ids": ["C87"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Dinoprost showed high rat jejunal effective permeability (1.46–2.57 × 10^-4 cm/s) at acidic pH and PGF2alpha was stable in intestinal lumen (<20% degradation in 30 min), supporting absorption of ionized prostaglandin acids.",
      "card_ids": ["C107", "C125", "C151"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "PGE2 is transported by the basolateral organic solute transporter Ostα/β, indicating carrier-mediated absorption of prostaglandin acids.",
      "card_ids": ["C154"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Asimadoline, a P-gp substrate, showed at least 20% absorption within 1 h in mice with plasma levels comparable to P-gp knockout, showing efflux does not necessarily limit net uptake below the F threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C175"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Pravastatin, an acidic drug with a Caco-2 efflux ratio of 2.7, still had an estimated fraction absorbed of 34% in 2/4/A1 cells, and compound 36 with an efflux ratio of 3.2 was classified as high absorption potential, indicating efflux alone does not imply F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C186", "C193", "C172"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Tafluprost, a prostaglandin ester prodrug, showed concentration-dependent rat intestinal absorption (P% 22.3 at 50 µg/mL decreasing to 11.4 at 150 µg/mL), but this is a prodrug with saturable absorption and does not directly apply to the query acid.",
      "card_ids": ["C192"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "gut_wall_efflux_intestinal_metabolism",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C154", "C175", "C186", "C172"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule.",
    "No matched oral-versus-IV study for the query.",
    "L5 records are for other prostaglandins/acids (PGE2, pravastatin, tafluprost), not the exact benzindene prostacyclin core.",
    "No direct evidence on treprostinil-specific gut-wall efflux or intestinal metabolism.",
    "Formulation and dose effects are unknown."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L5 adds mechanistic gut-wall transport/efflux evidence but no direct treprostinil F data. Positive records (PGE2 Ostα/β transport, asimadoline ≥20% absorption despite P-gp, pravastatin FA 34% despite efflux, compound 36 high absorption despite efflux) support that acidic prostaglandin analogs can achieve F ≥20%; potential negative records (pravastatin efflux, tafluprost concentration-dependent absorption) are for different molecules/prodrugs and do not overturn the cicaprost 100% F evidence. Prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

